  "query_preview": "..\nConfidence is increasing of a sustained trade-wind surge bringing \nbreezy winds with near-gale gusts to the region by early next week, \nas a result of an increasing pressure gradient between the mid- \nlatitudes and tropics. There is a chance of low-end scattered showers\nand isolated thunderstorms tonight through tomorrow afternoon, \nbefore generally drier weather moves in associated with the building \ntrade-winds. These winds will additionally make a fire weather watch \nand later a red flag warning likely Saturday morning, then Sunday \nmorning. This is because they will be accompanied by a drop in \ndewpoints which will lower the afternoon relative humidities.",
